# Local data files — financial exports and large PDFs (not for version control)
# (docs uses /* so specific source-of-record snapshots can be re-included below)
EV/
docs/*
# …except the SoCal county-onboarding runbook (Phase 52: the source-of-record
# procedure operators follow to add any CA county — a tracked deliverable)
!docs/socal-county-onboarding.md
# …and the v2.5 Utah source-of-record deliverables (Phase 68): the BigQuery access
# runbook + the confirmed 15-entity mapping that downstream Utah phases depend on.
!docs/utah-bigquery-access.md
!docs/utah-entity-mapping.md
!docs/utah-salaries-coverage.md
# …and the 50/50-ACFR end-state record (Phase 123, NASBORT-01): the durable source-of-record
# for the all-50-states-on-ACFR milestone + the two accepted NASBO fallback nodes.
!docs/state-acfr-5050.md
# …and the Federal Audit Clearinghouse extract that evidences every California
# city's fiscal-year end (2016-2025). This is not a convenience copy: it is the
# EVIDENCE the CA fiscal-calendar census is derived from, and
# tests/caFiscalYearCensus.test.mjs reads it — untracked, a fresh clone fails.
!docs/CA/
docs/CA/*
!docs/CA/fac-ca-city-fiscal-year-ends.csv
!docs/TX/
docs/TX/*
!docs/TX/fac-tx-local-fiscal-year-ends.csv
!docs/MD/
docs/MD/*
!docs/MD/fac-md-local-fiscal-year-ends.csv
# The FAC bulk download itself is 266 MB and is NEVER committed — regenerate the
# extracts above with `node scripts/buildFacFiscalYearCensus.mjs --download`.
.fac-general.csv

